// `iptmusic.com` — the four marketing and legal pages.
//
// **This repository exists only to be deployed.** The pages are generated in
// `SL-Collective/ipt` by `make site`, from `docs/privacy-policy.md`, `docs/terms.md` and
// `docs/refund-policy.md`, and checked there by `Tools/check_site_current.py`. Editing them here
// puts the published page out of step with the documents the product is written against — and the
// privacy policy is the one App Store Connect stores a URL for, so the copy strangers read would
// no longer be the copy this project checks.
//
// There is no build step and there is nothing to inject: four static pages, no credential, and the
// photograph is embedded. That is deliberate, so the pages Apple and Stripe read cannot be held
// offline by whether a build machine happens to have the right tools.
// `docs/` rather than `public/` because GitHub Pages accepts only `/` or `/docs` as a source, and
// Pages is already switched on for this repository. That gives the same four pages a second live
// address — `sl-collective.github.io/ipt-site/` — which is not the product's front door and is not
// meant to be: it is somewhere the owner can look at what is about to ship without waiting on a
// deployment nobody in this repository can trigger.
{
  "name": "ipt-site",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-21",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./docs",
    // `/privacy`, `/terms` and `/refunds` are directories holding an `index.html`, and Apple and
    // Stripe have each stored one of those bare paths. Explicit because two external reviews
    // depend on it, and a default is not a decision anybody wrote down.
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash"
  }
}
